Fillets: which corner failed at a faulty vertex, and why.

A fillet whose corner at a vertex fails tells the vertex (FaultyVertex),
and with patch 0320 Failure_Corner, but not which corner it tried there
nor why it failed: PerformFilletOnVertex builds a blend's end
(PerformOneCorner, a mitred end, an end over several surfdatas, an end
where more than three sharp edges meet), two or three blends meeting, more
blends or sharp edges, or blends ending in points, and each of these fails
with an exception whose message names the step (or is not done without
one). For each faulty vertex, ChFi3d_Builder::FailedCorner(IV) now gives
the corner (CornerKind), FailedCornerBlends(IV) and FailedCornerEdges(IV)
the blends and the sharp edges meeting there, and FailedCornerMessage(IV)
the exception's message, also through BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet. The
computation is unchanged.
